KG42.register("nodes-4c2b0a7939d48c4d4b720301",{"id":"KG31-36e0a27c810a788e","code":"OMC015.3","label":"Single trading intermediary with autonomous pricing","definition":"The organizer, as the internal unified buyer-seller counterparty, determines transaction prices according to its own economic objective; participants respond autonomously, and the organizer undertakes internal transactions and the external balancing interface.","layer":"L4","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"coordination.local_operator","concept_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Decision authority: the organizer holds internal pricing authority","Economic role: the organizer is a unified counterparty and pursues its own economic return","Interaction relation: price publication, autonomous response by participants, and result feedback"]},"exclusions":[["The MGO is the Stackelberg leader, and the participants are the set G of PV prosumers; the MGO pursues its own profit, and the prosumers pursue their respective utility.","The MGO receives prosumer consumption decisions and organizes PV sharing; when internal generation and consumption do not match, it bears the balancing responsibility for transactions with the utility grid.","The MGO deploys servers; the source implementation uses U-EMS, smart meters, and AMI communication.","The MGO purchases sellers' electricity at p_s and sells electricity to buyers at p_b.","Specific price-determination and transaction formulas are retained as responsibility context; the organizer role does not fabricate formulas or device control authority."]],"members":[{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The MGO coordinates and optimizes local PV energy sharing with the objective of maximizing its own profit. Scope: Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. The internal prices p_b and p_s determine the aggregate trading quantities E^b and E^s through the model's price-dependent consumption responses. Scope: Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. Condition: Trading quantities use the consumption response in (2), derived under E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0. The final ESM decision may be scheduled five minutes before the time slot. Scope: Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot. Condition: The monitoring and control system's communication latency is commonly less than several seconds.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. | Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. | Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E06"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"3a304bae600d1d987d8d474ca346ea7cc2f91c5ed85c15e75339662759cfeaeb","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002","node_id":"coordination.local_operator","function":"coordination.local_operator","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand. A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. | Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. | The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. | The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e021"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"0d8e892f31e0d5302dacb59afdc173bdc4228ba3a65407577a9a7b02d7bb6d8a","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003","node_id":"coordination.local_operator","function":"coordination.local_operator","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"05b2d6278d5d838a1db5a0b90bc1ed3377894510310873b8482301f4cdbf854d","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005","node_id":"coordination.local_operator","function":"coordination.local_operator","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. | Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. | Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. | Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b35948c248279327effe00aef49d47871e55293baf5b4fa11c535f5eaecf835b","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008","node_id":"coordination.local_operator","function":"coordination.local_operator","unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"sumers, the effective energy sharing management (ESM) E is important for the operation. In this pape","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":", g g y he as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). i- 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV syste","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each prosumer evaluates the flexible load of the next time slot, and decides the optimal energy consumption x_n^o. Every prosumer sends x_n^o to the MGO, the energy sharing of the next time slot is decided.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Each prosumer evaluates the flexible load of the next time slot, and decides the optimal energy consumption x_n^o. Every prosumer sends x_n^o to the MGO, the energy sharing of the next time slot is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"sumers, the effective energy sharing management (ESM) E is important for the operation. In this pape","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":", g g y he as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). i- 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV syste","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to implement the ESM, a server should be deployed in the MGO, while each prosumer should be deployed with the user energy management system (U-EMS) and smart meter. The information exchanges between MGO and prosumers can be realized via advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) system [25]. As we know, this is almost the basic configuration of applications in the Smart Grid.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In order to implement the ESM, a server should be deployed in the MGO, while each prosumer should be deployed with the user energy management system (U-EMS) and smart meter. The information exchanges between MGO and prosumers can be realized via advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) system [25]. As we know, this is almost the basic configuration of applications in the Smart Grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly.","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["leader_follower_operator_organization"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"KG31-L4-SC-L4-cd323306e2d3d0c1","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L4","ontological_kind":"SC-L4-cd323306e2d3d0c1"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"The organizer, as the internal unified buyer-seller counterparty, determines transaction prices according to its own economic objective; participants respond autonomously, and the organizer undertakes internal transactions and the external balancing interface.","identity_fields":["Decision authority: the organizer holds internal pricing authority","Economic role: the organizer is a unified counterparty and pursues its own economic return","Interaction relation: price publication, autonomous response by participants, and result feedback"]},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.local_operator","source_occurrences":[{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The MGO coordinates and optimizes local PV energy sharing with the objective of maximizing its own profit. Scope: Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. The internal prices p_b and p_s determine the aggregate trading quantities E^b and E^s through the model's price-dependent consumption responses. Scope: Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. Condition: Trading quantities use the consumption response in (2), derived under E_n^g − x_n ≠ 0. The final ESM decision may be scheduled five minutes before the time slot. Scope: Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot. Condition: The monitoring and control system's communication latency is commonly less than several seconds.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of aggregate local trading quantities in the Stackelberg energy-sharing model. | Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid. | Implementation timing of the final local energy-sharing decision for a forthcoming time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E06"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"3a304bae600d1d987d8d474ca346ea7cc2f91c5ed85c15e75339662759cfeaeb"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand. A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. | Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. | The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. | The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e021"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","source_rule_sha256":"0d8e892f31e0d5302dacb59afdc173bdc4228ba3a65407577a9a7b02d7bb6d8a"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0 Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"05b2d6278d5d838a1db5a0b90bc1ed3377894510310873b8482301f4cdbf854d"},{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots. The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots. Internal buying and selling prices are decision variables for maximizing the MGO's own profit, subject to λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization. Initial internal selling and buying prices may be set to λ^s and λ^b, respectively. Scope: Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. Condition: Initial price setting. Select the internal price pair by comparing MGO profit at the optima of D_1 and D_2, where D_1 applies when E^b \u003c E^s and D_2 applies when E^b ≥ E^s. Scope: Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. The internal selling and buying prices remain at λ^s and λ^b, respectively, in these reported time slots. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. Condition: PV energy is entirely self-consumed and no energy is feasible to trade inside the microgrid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Initialization of internal prices for each time slot. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. | Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 7 and 17–19 only. | Selection of optimal internal prices across the surplus and nonsurplus pricing regions. | Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot. | Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"b35948c248279327effe00aef49d47871e55293baf5b4fa11c535f5eaecf835b"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO coordinates and optimizes local PV energy sharing with the objective of maximizing its own profit. Scope: Hour-ahead energy-sharing management among PV prosumers within one microgrid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"sumers, the effective energy sharing management (ESM) E is important for the operation. In this pape","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":", g g y he as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). i- 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV syste","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each prosumer evaluates the flexible load of the next time slot, and decides the optimal energy consumption x_n^o. Every prosumer sends x_n^o to the MGO, the energy sharing of the next time slot is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"sumers, the effective energy sharing management (ESM) E is important for the operation. In this pape","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":", g g y he as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). i- 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV syste","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e021"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to implement the ESM, a server should be deployed in the MGO, while each prosumer should be deployed with the user energy management system (U-EMS) and smart meter. The information exchanges between MGO and prosumers can be realized via advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) system [25]. As we know, this is almost the basic configuration of applications in the Smart Grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. Scope: Stackelberg leader-follower coordination in the ESM arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e006"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer must sell its net surplus to the MGO, which purchases seller energy at the internal selling price p_s. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n > 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n > 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(E_n^g - x_n \\text{ is sold to the MGO at } p_s\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under the source's nonpositive-net-energy branch, the prosumer must buy its net energy requirement from the MGO, which sells buyer energy at the internal buying price p_b. Scope: Internal PV energy exchange between a prosumer and the MGO in one time slot. Condition: E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0","expression":"\\forall n\\in G:\\; E_n^g - x_n \\le 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\bigl(x_n - E_n^g \\text{ is bought from the MGO at } p_b\\bigr)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R005-x-x_n"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","v141-c-R005-theta-p_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e014"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e012","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define G as the set of PV prosumers inside the microgrid. Let B and S be the set of buyers and the set sellers, respectively. We denote that there are N = |G| prosumers, N_B = |B| buyers, N_S = |S| sellers in the microgrid, and there is N = N_B + N_S. Each prosumer n ∈ G can produce energy E_n^g and consume energy x_n in one time slot. Then the prosumer n needs to trade energy E_n^g − x_n with MGO. If E_n^g − x_n > 0, the prosumer n sell energy to MGO. Otherwise, the prosumer n buy energy from MGO as E_n^g − x_n ≤ 0."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO determines the internal buying and selling prices simultaneously and obtains next-slot prices by solving the pricing optimization. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal buying and selling prices for the next time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e019"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e019","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Considering (26) and (27) belong to nonlinear programming problem, the MGO can solve (30) and obtain the internal prices p_s and p_b for the next time slot by using interior point method. The MGO broadcasts the internal prices of next time slot to all the prosumers;"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO increases the internal selling price p_s in the reported shortage cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16. Condition: Selling energy is less than buying energy in these reported time slots.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E12"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO decreases the internal buying price p_b in the reported surplus cases. Scope: Reported Stackelberg case study, time slots 13 and 14. Condition: Selling energy is more than buying energy in these reported time slots.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E12"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.B Analysis of the Internal Prices","anchor_text":"en re Fig. 9. Comparison of net energy. is D First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"First, in time slots 10, 11, 12, and 16, as the amount of selling energy is less than the buying energy, the MGO increases the selling price p_{s} and motivates the sellers to sell more energy; and second, in time slots 13 and 14, as the amount of selling energy is more than the buying energy, the MGO decreases the buying price p_{b}, and thus the buyers are encouraged to consume more extra PV energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The MGO profit objective for internal-price optimization is the piecewise function R(p_b,p_s) in (5): it collects p_b E^b from buyers and pays p_s E^s to sellers, and settles the net imbalance with the utility grid at λ^s when E^s > E^b or at λ^b when E^s ≤ E^b. Scope: Stackelberg ESM internal-price optimization.","expression":"R(p_b,p_s)=\\begin{cases} p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^s(E^s-E^b), & E^s>E^b,\\\\ p_b E^b - p_s E^s + \\lambda^b(E^s-E^b), & E^s\\le E^b. \\end{cases}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["x_p_b","x_p_s"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_s","theta_lambda_b"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e007"],"ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e014","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.B Profit Model of MGO","anchor_text":"( n n) ( ) act n∈B ave Es = (Egn −xn). (4) n∈S 0 In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosum","equation_id":"(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In order to maximize PV energy sharing among prosumers, the profit function of the MGO is formulated as R(p_b, p_s) = { p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^s(E^s − E^b), E^s > E^b; p_b E^b − p_s E^s + λ^b(E^s − E^b), E^s ≤ E^b } (5) where the internal prices p_b and p_s are decision variables. MGO sells energy to buyers with price p_b and purchases energy from sellers with price p_s, which also trade with the utility grid simultaneously in order to keep the supply–demand balance in the microgrid. If E^s > E^b, MGO sells surplus PV energy to the utility grid with export price λ^s. Otherwise, MGO purchases energy from the utility grid with import price λ^b to meet the load demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e007","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":"imize the own proﬁt under constraint λ ≤ps \u003c pb ≤λ . The sl prosumers can get beneﬁts from the energ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In order to coordinate the sharing process among the prosumers, the internal selling (p_s) and buying prices (p_b) are set by the MGO. According to the feed-in tariff of some countries, the import and export prices between MGO and utility grid are constant. Generally, the export price λ^s is lower than the import price λ^b for encouraging local consumption of PV energy, and thus reduce the impact on the utility grid. The goal of MGO is to maximize the own profit under constraint λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b. The prosumers can get benefits from the energy sharing compared to trade with the utility grid directly."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x001","symbol":"x_n^o","meaning":"Optimal/chosen energy consumption of prosumer n for the next time slot, submitted to the MGO.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy-consumption quantity for prosumer n in the next time slot; the cited passage does not state numerical bounds for x_n^o, while the underlying consumption decision is bounded by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max.","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e015"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x001"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R005-x-x_n","symbol":"x_n","meaning":"Energy consumed by prosumer n in one time slot; it determines the prosumer's net trade E_n^g - x_n with the MGO.","kind":"operational","domain":"n ∈ G (set of PV prosumers); prosumer energy consumption in one time slot; no explicit numeric bounds are stated in the supplied R005 evidence","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-x_n"},{"variable_id":"x_p_s","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price set by the MGO for the next time slot; a decision variable in the MGO profit-maximization and bounded by the internal-price constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"real scalar per time slot; λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":["time slot"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::x::x_p_s"},{"variable_id":"x_p_b","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price set by the MGO for the next time slot; a decision variable in the MGO profit-maximization and bounded by the internal-price constraint.","kind":"operational","domain":"real scalar per time slot; λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b","unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":["time slot"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g01-e014","v141-b-g01-e019"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::x::x_p_b"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g","symbol":"E_n^g","meaning":"Energy produced by prosumer n in the same time slot; input to the net trade E_n^g - x_n.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-E_n^g"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-p_s","symbol":"p_s","meaning":"Internal selling price at which the MGO purchases seller energy in this execution branch; treated as an input price for this activation-stage rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_s"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R005-theta-p_b","symbol":"p_b","meaning":"Internal buying price at which the MGO sells buyer energy in this execution branch; treated as an input price for this activation-stage rule.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e014"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-p_b"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_s","symbol":"λ^s","meaning":"Utility-grid export (feed-in) price; constant export price, lower than import price λ^b. Case-study calibration λ^s = 0.4 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":0.4,"text_value":null},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_s"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_b","symbol":"λ^b","meaning":"Utility-grid import price; constant import price, higher than export price λ^s. Case-study calibration λ^b = 1.0 CNY/kWh.","value":{"kind":"numeric","number_value":1.0,"text_value":null},"unit":"CNY/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e007","v141-b-g02-E01"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_b"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","stage":"L4","subtype":"leader_follower_operator_organization","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The MGO, as the Stackelberg leader and internal unified counterparty, is responsible for determining the internal dual prices, receiving prosumer consumption decisions, and organizing PV sharing; prosumers respond autonomously as followers.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: decision relationship between the organizer and participants","Core relation: the organizer holds pricing authority; participants respond autonomously and return consumption decisions","Output: explicit organizational rights and responsibilities, leader-follower relationship, and internal counterparty"],"variation_fields":["The organizer is the MGO, and the participants are the set G of PV prosumers","The MGO pursues its own profit; prosumers pursue their respective utility","When internal generation and consumption do not match, the MGO bears the balancing responsibility for transactions with the utility grid","The MGO deploys servers; the source implementation uses U-EMS, smart meters, and AMI communication","The MGO purchases sellers' electricity at p_s and sells electricity to buyers at p_b; the specific price-determination and transaction formulas are retained as responsibility context"],"constraint_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C004","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C005","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C002","14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001"],"paper_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"coordination.local_operator","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","retained_variants":["The MGO is the Stackelberg leader, and the participants are the set G of PV prosumers; the MGO pursues its own profit, and the prosumers pursue their respective utility.","The MGO receives prosumer consumption decisions and organizes PV sharing; when internal generation and consumption do not match, it bears the balancing responsibility for transactions with the utility grid.","The MGO deploys servers; the source implementation uses U-EMS, smart meters, and AMI communication.","The MGO purchases sellers' electricity at p_s and sells electricity to buyers at p_b.","Specific price-determination and transaction formulas are retained as responsibility context; the organizer role does not fabricate formulas or device control authority."],"evidence_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator::projection"]}],"functional":{"is_child":true,"subdivision_pending":false,"baseline_parent_id":"COMP-f9e3ecd5613f7b1a","baseline_parent_code":"OMC015","secondary_class":"SC-L4-cd323306e2d3d0c1","category":{"id":"SC-L4-cd323306e2d3d0c1","stage":"L4","label_zh":"Single trading intermediary with autonomous pricing","definition_zh":"The organizer, as the internal unified buyer-seller counterparty, determines transaction prices according to its own economic objective; participants respond autonomously, and the organizer undertakes internal transactions and the external balancing interface.","main_identity_axes":["Decision authority: the organizer determines internal prices","Economic role: a unified counterparty pursuing its own economic return","Interaction relation: pricing leader and autonomously responding participants"],"inclusion_criteria":["The organizer simultaneously has internal pricing authority and unified-counterparty status","The organizer sets prices according to its own economic objective, and participants retain decision-making authority to respond"],"exclusion_criteria":["Only entrusted to run a fixed pricing model","Only represents members in internal organization and external purchase/sale","Only acts as a third party organizing auctions without unified-counterparty status","Directly controls participating devices through operating instructions"],"supporting_unit_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator"],"status":"agent_defined_structurally_validated"},"definition":{"definition_zh":"The organizer, as the internal unified buyer-seller counterparty, determines transaction prices according to its own economic objective; participants respond autonomously, and the organizer undertakes internal transactions and the external balancing interface.","identity_fields":["Decision authority: the organizer holds internal pricing authority","Economic role: the organizer is a unified counterparty and pursues its own economic return","Interaction relation: price publication, autonomous response by participants, and result feedback"],"member_unit_ids":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator"]}},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/309"});
